---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../data/assets';

const title = 'Do Not Farm Grave Seasons Before the Price';
const description =
  'Grave Seasons has no US price on the October 26 Steam check. Do not plan a farm, a romance, or a killer route from a leak.';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'No price yet', url: '/no-price-before-the-farm/' },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} image={ASSETS.steamHeader.src}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <p class="section-kicker">Checked October 26, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black leading-tight text-bone md:text-5xl">No price. No farm plan.</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-fog">
      The October 26, 2026 US check of Steam App 3255110 did not print a price. The page is still
      coming soon, dated March 9, 2027. A spreadsheet of crop days is not a substitute for that button.
    </p>
    <figure class="mt-8">
      <img src={ASSETS.steamHeader.src} alt={ASSETS.steamHeader.alt} width={ASSETS.steamHeader.width} height={ASSETS.steamHeader.height} class="rounded-md border border-white/10" loading="eager" />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-xs text-fog">Steam header for Grave Seasons.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="mt-8 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-fog">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-bone">What you can record now</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li>The pitch: a narrative farming sim in Ashenridge, with a supernatural serial killer.</li>
        <li>One year to protect victims. Farming, foraging, crafting, and investigation are the named tools.</li>
        <li>Genres on the listing: Indie, RPG, Simulation. The 12 romance names stay on their own page.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-bone">What you cannot record</h2>
      <p>
        Stamina, shop hours, seed prices, and which resident is safe are not published. Day 1 Xbox
        Game Pass is a subscription row, not a Steam price. File size is still on
        <a class="text-wheat underline" href="/price-and-file-size/">price and file size</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        When the button prints a number, buy or wait. Until then, the useful pre-launch act is a
        resident list with a source, not a fake day-one route.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
